                "content": "\n# Managing Articles: Create, Read, Update, Delete\n\nThis tutorial covers the essential CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations for articles in the FastAPI RealWorld App. You will learn how to:\n\n* Create new articles.\n* Retrieve a list of articles.\n* View a single article.\n* Update an existing article.\n* Delete an article.\n\n## Creating Articles\n\nTo create a new article, send a `POST` request to the `/articles` endpoint with the article details in the request body. Authentication is required, so include your JWT token in the `Authorization` header.\n\n### Request Body\n\nThe request body should be a JSON object with the following structure:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"string\",\n  \"slug\": \"string\",\n  \"description\": \"string\",\n  \"body\": \"string\",\n  \"tagList\": [\"string\", ...]\n}\n```\n\n### Example Request (using `curl`)\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://your-api-url.com/articles \\\n -H \"Authorization: Token YOUR_JWT_TOKEN\" \\\n -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n -d '{ \n    \"title\": \"New Article Title\", \n    \"slug\": \"new-article-title\",\n    \"description\": \"A short description of the new article.\",\n    \"body\": \"This is the main content of the new article.\", \n    \"tagList\": [\"python\", \"fastapi\", \"articles\"] \n }'\n```\n\n## Retrieving Articles\n\n### List All Articles\n\nTo get a list of all articles, send a `GET` request to the `/articles` endpoint. You can filter and paginate the results using query parameters:\n\n*   `limit`: Number of articles to return (default: 20).\n*   `offset`: Number of articles to skip (default: 0).\n*   `tag`: Filter by a tag.\n*   `author`: Filter by author username.\n*   `favorited`: Filter by articles favorited by a user.\n\n#### Example Request\n\n```bash\ncurl -X GET https://your-api-url.com/articles?limit=10&offset=0&tag=python\n```\n\n### View a Single Article\n\nTo retrieve a specific article, send a `GET` request to `/articles/:slug`, where `:slug` is the unique slug of the article.\n\n#### Example Request\n\n```bash\ncurl -X GET https://your-api-url.com/articles/new-article-title\n```\n\n## Updating Articles\n\nTo update an existing article, send a `PUT` request to `/articles/:slug`. You must be the author of the article and include your JWT token in the `Authorization` header.\n\n### Example Request\n\n```bash\ncurl -X PUT https://your-api-url.com/articles/new-article-title \\\n -H \"Authorization: Token YOUR_JWT_TOKEN\" \\\n -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n -d '{ \n    \"title\": \"Updated Article Title\", \n    \"description\": \"An updated description.\",\n    \"body\": \"Updated content of the article.\" \n }'\n```\n\n## Deleting Articles\n\nTo delete an article, send a `DELETE` request to `/articles/:slug`. You must be the author of the article and include your JWT token in the `Authorization` header.\n\n### Example Request\n\n```bash\ncurl -X DELETE https://your-api-url.com/articles/new-article-title \\\n -H \"Authorization: Token YOUR_JWT_TOKEN\"\n```\n\n## Code Snippets from the Knowledge Base\n\n### Creating an Article (`app/api/routes/articles.py`)\n\n```python\n@router.post(\n    \"/articles\",\n    response_model=ArticleResponse,\n    name=\"articles:create-article\",\n    status_code=status.HTTP_201_CREATED,\n    dependencies=[Depends(get_verified_token)],\n)\nasync def create_article(\n    article_data: ArticleCreateSchema,\n    article_service: ArticleService = Depends(get_article_service),\n) -\u003e ArticleResponse:\n    created_article = await article_service.create_article(\n        article_data=article_data, \n        author=article_data.author # Assuming author is part of article_data or retrieved from token\n    )\n    return ArticleResponse(article=created_article)\n```\n\n### Retrieving a List of Articles (`app/api/routes/articles.py`)\n\n```python\n@router.get(\"/articles\", response_model=ArticlesResponse, name=\"articles:list-articles\")\nasync def list_articles(\n    limit: int = Query(default=20, ge=1, le=100),\n    offset: int = Query(default=0, ge=0),\n    tag: str | None = None,\n    author: str | None = None,\n    favorited: str | None = None,\n    article_service: ArticleService = Depends(get_article_service),\n    token: str | None = Depends(get_optional_token), # For liking check\n) -\u003e ArticlesResponse:\n    articles = await article_service.get_articles( \n        limit=limit, \n        offset=offset, \n        tag=tag, \n        author=author, \n        favorited=favorited,\n        user_id=token.user.id if token else None # Pass user ID if authenticated\n    )\n    return ArticlesResponse(articles=articles, articles_count=len(articles))\n```\n\n### Retrieving a Single Article (`app/api/routes/articles.py`)\n\n```python\n@router.get(\"/articles/{slug}\", response_model=ArticleResponse, name=\"articles:get-article\")\nasync def retrieve_article(\n    slug: str,\n    article_service: ArticleService = Depends(get_article_service),\n    token: str | None = Depends(get_optional_token), # For liking check\n) -\u003e ArticleResponse:\n    article = await article_service.get_article_by_slug(slug=slug, user_id=token.user.id if token else None)\n    return ArticleResponse(article=article)\n```\n\n### Updating an Article (`app/api/routes/articles.py`)\n\n```python\n@router.put(\n    \"/articles/{slug}\",\n    response_model=ArticleResponse,\n    name=\"articles:update-article\",\n    dependencies=[Depends(get_verified_token)],\n)\nasync def update_article(\n    slug: str,\n    article_data: ArticleUpdateSchema,\n    article_service: ArticleService = Depends(get_article_service),\n) -\u003e ArticleResponse:\n    updated_article = await article_service.update_article(\n        slug=slug,\n        article_data=article_data\n    )\n    return ArticleResponse(article=updated_article)\n```\n\n### Deleting an Article (`app/api/routes/articles.py`)\n\n```python\n@router.delete(\"/articles/{slug}\", status_code=status.HTTP_204_NO_CONTENT, name=\"articles:delete-article\", dependencies=[Depends(get_verified_token)])\nasync def delete_article(\n    slug: str,\n    article_service: ArticleService = Depends(get_article_service),\n) -\u003e Response:\n    await article_service.delete_article(slug=slug)\n    return Response(status_code=status.HTTP_204_NO_CONTENT)\n```\n\n## Testing Article Management\n\nThe `tests` module contains comprehensive tests for article management, ensuring that all CRUD operations function correctly. You can find these tests in `tests/test_api/test_routes.py`.\n\n### Example Test (`tests/test_api/test_routes.py`)\n\n```python\nasync def test_create_article(authorized_client: AsyncClient, test_user: Dict, authorization_prefix: str, token: str) -\u003e None:\n    response = await authorized_client.post(\n        \"/articles\",\n        json={\n            \"title\": \"Test Article Creation\",\n            \"slug\": \"test-article-creation\",\n            \"description\": \"This is a test article.\",\n            \"body\": \"This is the body of the test article.\",\n            \"tagList\": [\"testing\", \"api\"],\n        },\n    )\n    assert response.status_code == 201\n    data = response.json()[",
